## 3. Fresh exact dyadic endpoint enclosure

Set S=2^768 and N=320, with eight steps of length 1/8 in each slot. These
choices were frozen before execution. A complex rectangle is represented
by four integer endpoints divided by S, ordered
(real_lo,real_hi,imag_lo,imag_hi). Addition is exact. Real interval products
take minima/maxima of the four integer corner products; complex products
enclose ac-bd and ad+bc, then divide outward by S. Division by positive d
uses floor n//d and ceiling -((-n)//d). Multiplication by a signed Gaussian
integer first swaps endpoints as required by the signs, with no rounding.
All integer arithmetic uses arbitrary-precision Python integers.

At step start x=k/8, the shifted quartic has exact coefficients

    p0=16x^2(1-x)^2,
    p1=32x(1-x)(1-2x),
    p2=16-96x+96x^2,
    p3=-32+64x, p4=16.

Writing A(z)=-i[K+a psi(x+z)P], its coefficients are exact Gaussian
rationals. The code selects their common positive denominator, stores
sparse Gaussian-integer numerators, and uses the exact recurrence

    U_0=I,
    (m+1)U_(m+1)=sum_(k=0)^min(4,m) A_k U_(m-k).                    (3)

Each sparse left product and sum is accumulated in integers before one
outward division by denominator*(m+1). Thus induction encloses the exact
Taylor coefficients, not approximations with empirically estimated error.
Horner evaluation at 1/8 divides outward at each stage. Steps compose by
left multiplication in chronological order, then all 24 slot endpoints
compose in the same order. Associativity identifies the resulting exact
truncated product Uhat with the ordered product of the 192 truncated steps.
Arithmetic enclosures may overestimate dependencies but never identify
independently varying rectangle entries with a smaller uncertainty set.

The analytic tail is priced separately. The conservative polynomial

    b(z)=7+32z+64z^2+128z^3+64z^4

majorizes ||A_k||: ||K||=3, ||P||=2, a<1, and the shifted coefficient
bounds are 1,8,16,32,16. This is looser than needed for the U-only problem
but remains valid. The scalar solution f(z)=exp(integral_0^z b) has
nonnegative coefficients and majorizes all matrix coefficient norms in
(3). At R=1/4,

    integral_0^R b=773/240<4,   f(R)<e^4<81.

The elementary factorial-series bound e<3 suffices. At h=R/2, every
omitted term past degree 320 gains at least 2^-321, so

    ||U_step-P_320(h)|| <= delta=81/2^321.                         (4)

The exact U-only segment propagators are unitary, including all scalar
phases. Telescoping approximate prefixes against exact suffixes gives

    E_m <= delta sum_(k=0)^(m-1)(1+E_k)
         <=(1+delta)^m-1
         <=m delta exp(m delta)<2m delta,        m<=192.

Here m delta<1/2 and exp(1/2)<2. Consequently

    ||Uhat-U0|| <= e0=384delta=31104/2^321.                         (5)

The stored rectangle encloses Uhat itself; its rounding width is already
present and is not absorbed into, or omitted from, e0. All 24 slot
rectangles and the complete endpoint rectangle are retained. No entry from
